INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(6355338, 939629, 19825, '<td valign="top">I was going back through the Tarot entries, and I cannot believe how harsh voters were on this image. I really liked it and scored it much higher. I think the crop is good -- it conveys the feeling of closeness in a subway car. His focus on the book and the motion in the window. Nice shot.</td>', 'I was going back through the Tarot entries, and I cannot believe how harsh voters were on this image. I really liked it and scored it much higher. I think the crop is good -- it conveys the feeling of closeness in a subway car. His focus on the book and the motion in the window. Nice shot.', '2011-03-17 22:08:41.000000', NULL, 0),
(6355518, 939786, 54645, '<td valign="top">Excellent. That eye socket is disturbing.</td>', 'Excellent. That eye socket is disturbing.', '2011-03-18 00:06:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6355643, 939013, 129881, '<td valign="top">If my seer were to draw the tower, I would feel exactly how this image makes me feel. Visually appealing? Sure. But anyone can do that. You''ve managed to capture an image that crosses over from the visual to the kinesthetic. If I printed tarot decks for a living, I''d ask if I could put this on the back of the tower card. Congratulations - it''s perfect.</td>', 'If my seer were to draw the tower, I would feel exactly how this image makes me feel. Visually appealing? Sure. But anyone can do that. You''ve managed to capture an image that crosses over from the visual to the kinesthetic. If I printed tarot decks for a living, I''d ask if I could put this on the back of the tower card. Congratulations - it''s perfect.', '2011-03-18 01:20:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(6355646, 939317, 129881, '<td valign="top">Thoroughly average worldly old man picture.<br/> <br/>However, unlike a gypsy or any other 3rd world oddity, this is just a regular guy in a costume. You found a regular guy - someone just like you or me - and made him look like a star. You took Joe and made him in to King Henry.<br/> <br/>How often do you get to do that?</td>', 'Thoroughly average worldly old man picture. However, unlike a gypsy or any other 3rd world oddity, this is just a regular guy in a costume. You found a regular guy - someone just like you or me - and made him look like a star. You took Joe and made him in to King Henry. How often do you get to do that?', '2011-03-18 01:24:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(6355652, 939818, 30982, '<td valign="top">OK, the crown made me laugh out loud.  Looks like one of the Burger King crowns, only bigger!  :-)  Top ten, and 6+ though, so you can''t complain!  And good to see you, too.</td>', 'OK, the crown made me laugh out loud.  Looks like one of the Burger King crowns, only bigger!  :-)  Top ten, and 6+ though, so you can''t complain!  And good to see you, too.', '2011-03-18 01:35:42.000000', NULL, 0),
(6355653, 939796, 129881, '<td valign="top">This better show up in learn-&gt;how\''d they do that. It\''s rare for a photograph to just seem completely separate from the laws of light, but you\\\\\\\''ve done it.<br/> <br/>Now, one problem: DNMC. I\''m sure you did your research before you went to all this work. You don\''t look like a girl. WoF card must have a girl. Also, I don\''t see TARO or ROTA. Nor do I see all four elements or the fates or really anything related to the wheel of fortune tarot card.<br/> <br/>That\''s unfortunate because this is a spectacular image.<br/> <br/>So let us know just how exactly it is that this image has ANYTHING to do with the WoF TC.</td>', 'This better show up in learn->how\''d they do that. It\''s rare for a photograph to just seem completely separate from the laws of light, but you\\\\\\\''ve done it. Now, one problem: DNMC. I\''m sure you did your research before you went to all this work. You don\''t look like a girl. WoF card must have a girl. Also, I don\''t see TARO or ROTA. Nor do I see all four elements or the fates or really anything related to the wheel of fortune tarot card. That\''s unfortunate because this is a spectacular image. So let us know just how exactly it is that this image has ANYTHING to do with the WoF TC.', '2011-03-18 01:36:34.000000', NULL, 0),
(6355659, 939669, 129881, '<td valign="top">HOLY HELL DEATH IS A GIRL????<br/>How did you even get that spot? Ridiculous!!!<br/> <br/>A stellar image. I would have lit the candle and shot with ambient light + slight fill flash, but heinsight is 20/20. This image makes me feel like all the happiness is gone from the world. Love it. Amazing. Awesome.</td>', 'HOLY HELL DEATH IS A GIRL????How did you even get that spot? Ridiculous!!! A stellar image. I would have lit the candle and shot with ambient light + slight fill flash, but heinsight is 20/20. This image makes me feel like all the happiness is gone from the world. Love it. Amazing. Awesome.', '2011-03-18 01:52:06.000000', NULL, 0),
(6355664, 939756, 129881, '<td valign="top">First of all, the cleavage issue. The female fool is not a dignified woman; do your research!<br/>Second, a fool would NEVER wear purple.<br/>Third, the lack of even lighting makes her look like a man.<br/> <br/>Back to the cleavage issue, she''s not 19. If you''re 25 or older, it''s not called cleavage; it''s just a low-cut shirt.<br/> <br/>Oh and fourth, I can''t think of a way to possibly improve this image. It''s amazing and it captures the essence that it was meant to capture as well as it could be captured. Beautiful image and the photographer in me wants to meet the model because we all could use a model that''s not only beautiful, but has the guts to pose in any pose we ask for any shoot we ask. Could anyone else have executed this particular shoot this well? Doubtful. Aside from photographic and historical accuracy, this model is obviously quite an amazing person as well. I''m glad to have the opportunity to observe her at work; it''s changed my perception of the concept of a model completely. Excellent work, yo_spiff and my hat is off to the model.</td>', 'First of all, the cleavage issue. The female fool is not a dignified woman; do your research!Second, a fool would NEVER wear purple.Third, the lack of even lighting makes her look like a man. Back to the cleavage issue, she''s not 19. If you''re 25 or older, it''s not called cleavage; it''s just a low-cut shirt. Oh and fourth, I can''t think of a way to possibly improve this image. It''s amazing and it captures the essence that it was meant to capture as well as it could be captured. Beautiful image and the photographer in me wants to meet the model because we all could use a model that''s not only beautiful, but has the guts to pose in any pose we ask for any shoot we ask. Could anyone else have executed this particular shoot this well? Doubtful. Aside from photographic and historical accuracy, this model is obviously quite an amazing person as well. I''m glad to have the opportunity to observe her at work; it''s changed my perception of the concept of a model completely. Excellent work, yo_spiff and my hat is off to the model.', '2011-03-18 02:06:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(6355668, 939357, 129881, '<td valign="top">This entire image is completely devoid of depth. Except for the cloud. The modesty and humility of this image moved me.<br/> <br/>Oh, and as for the tilted comment - yes, I find the image to be significantly off. It seems like it might be flat relative to the horizon which makes the mountain look not only "off", but difficult to focus on. The cloud is even worse. The composition, on the other hand, which is what the eye of any true photographer will see, is perfect.<br/> <br/>Perhaps the other voters didn''t notice, but I think this is too subtle to ribbon. Take a deep breath before you look at it - it''s perfect.</td>', 'This entire image is completely devoid of depth. Except for the cloud. The modesty and humility of this image moved me. Oh, and as for the tilted comment - yes, I find the image to be significantly off. It seems like it might be flat relative to the horizon which makes the mountain look not only "off", but difficult to focus on. The cloud is even worse. The composition, on the other hand, which is what the eye of any true photographer will see, is perfect. Perhaps the other voters didn''t notice, but I think this is too subtle to ribbon. Take a deep breath before you look at it - it''s perfect.', '2011-03-18 02:11:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(6355671, 939828, 129881, '<td valign="top">The two-light setup reflection in her eyes says basic editing..<br/>But the vibrance in her tats says advanced editing. Well done.<br/> <br/>However, the image says "the fool" and the caption says "high priestess". The image is wonderful, but I''m unclear what relation this woman has with the "high priestess". The high priestess is a very sobering, somber card. This is neither.</td>', 'The two-light setup reflection in her eyes says basic editing..But the vibrance in her tats says advanced editing. Well done. However, the image says "the fool" and the caption says "high priestess". The image is wonderful, but I''m unclear what relation this woman has with the "high priestess". The high priestess is a very sobering, somber card. This is neither.', '2011-03-18 02:17:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(6355673, 939822, 129881, '<td valign="top">I''d give this one a ten just because I don''t think I''ve ever heard someone say etymologically.<br/>The devil''s advocate would say it looks like he''s trying to hide his holey.<br/>The ornithologist would ask why "he" has a holey.<br/>The philosopher would ask why you''re trying to shoot his holey.<br/>And I just really can''t get past that. Why were you trying to shoot his holey?<br/> <br/>Anyways, typical adjective for owls: "wise"<br/>Rough translation of hierophant: The one who shows you the way<br/>Anyways, lose the border and I''d say it''s top 10.</td>', 'I''d give this one a ten just because I don''t think I''ve ever heard someone say etymologically.The devil''s advocate would say it looks like he''s trying to hide his holey.The ornithologist would ask why "he" has a holey.The philosopher would ask why you''re trying to shoot his holey.And I just really can''t get past that. Why were you trying to shoot his holey? Anyways, typical adjective for owls: "wise"Rough translation of hierophant: The one who shows you the wayAnyways, lose the border and I''d say it''s top 10.', '2011-03-18 02:24:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(6355783, 939041, 108069, '<td valign="top">Well I would say it''s been a good week! Wonderful photo, again.</td>', 'Well I would say it''s been a good week! Wonderful photo, again.', '2011-03-18 08:20:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(6356307, 939317, 24454, '<td valign="top">Verrry nice!  I love the jovial spirit you captured. So many of these types of portraits are so serious.  This is delightful!  Congratulations on your red ribbon!</td>', 'Verrry nice!  I love the jovial spirit you captured. So many of these types of portraits are so serious.  This is delightful!  Congratulations on your red ribbon!', '2011-03-18 18:09:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(6356567, 939756, 118890, '<td valign="top">Howdy folks, this is the model speaking,<br/> <br/>This was a great shoot, and Steve was very fun to work with!  I love making funny faces, and so I was doubly-excited that Steve could find some way to work this unusual talent of mine into a relevant photo.  Sorry about the cleavage, though, next time I''ll put on a burka ;)<br/> <br/>Way to go Steve for pulling an awesome shot completely out of thin air!<br/></td>', 'Howdy folks, this is the model speaking, This was a great shoot, and Steve was very fun to work with!  I love making funny faces, and so I was doubly-excited that Steve could find some way to work this unusual talent of mine into a relevant photo.  Sorry about the cleavage, though, next time I''ll put on a burka ;) Way to go Steve for pulling an awesome shot completely out of thin air!', '2011-03-19 01:25:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(6356701, 939476, 103142, '<td valign="top">Awesome!! Congrats on your first top 10!!</td>', 'Awesome!! Congrats on your first top 10!!', '2011-03-19 06:47:55.000000', NULL, 0),
